#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# plot

#% text
# `plot(f, [x, a, b])` draws the curve of `f` for `x` from `a` to `b` as an image.

#% text
# `plot([f1, f2, ...], [x, a, b])` draws several curves in one picture, each in its own colour.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The value is `image("path")`, a PNG file; the notebook and this documentation show it in place.

#% item
# The function is sampled adaptively: evenly at first, then more densely where the curve bends.

#% item
# Where `f` is not a finite real number, or jumps by more than the visible range (at a pole), the curve is broken.

#% item
# The vertical range is chosen so that a few extreme values do not flatten the rest of the curve.

#% item
# Options:

#% subitem
# `x_label: "text"` and `y_label: "text"` label the axes.

#% subitem
# `legend: ["text", ...]` names the curves; `legend_position: top_right | top_left | bottom_left | bottom_right` places the box.

#% subitem
# `colors: ["#rrggbb", ...]` and `line_style: [solid | dashed | dotted | dot_dashed, ...]` set the look of each curve.

#% subitem
# `x_scale` and `y_scale`: `linear`, `log`, or `signed_log`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# One period of the sine:

#% cell
plot(sin(x), [x, 0, 2pi])
#% output
#= image("plot.files/plot-1.png")

#% text
# Two curves together:

#% cell
plot([sin(x), cos(x)], [x, 0, 2pi])
#% output
#= image("plot.files/plot-2.png")

#% text
# A polynomial with its three real roots:

#% cell
plot(x^3 - 3x, [x, -2.5, 2.5])
#% output
#= image("plot.files/plot-3.png")

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Poles break the curve instead of joining its branches:

#% cell
plot(tan(x), [x, -3, 3])
#% output
#= image("plot.files/plot-4.png")

#% text
# A function with a rapid oscillation near zero; sampling refines there:

#% cell
plot(x*sin(1/x), [x, -0.5, 0.5])
#% output
#= image("plot.files/plot-5.png")

#% subsection
# Options

#% text
# Labels and a legend:

#% cell
plot([exp(-x), exp(-2x)], [x, 0, 3], x_label: "t", y_label: "amount", legend: ["rate 1", "rate 2"])
#% output
#= image("plot.files/plot-6.png")

#% text
# A logarithmic vertical axis turns exponentials into straight lines:

#% cell
plot([exp(x), exp(2x)], [x, 0, 5], y_scale: log)
#% output
#= image("plot.files/plot-7.png")

#% text
# Colours and line styles:

#% cell
plot([sin(x), sin(2x)], [x, 0, pi], colors: ["#e45649", "#4078f2"], line_style: [solid, dashed])
#% output
#= image("plot.files/plot-8.png")

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# A function and its derivative:

#% cell
plot([x*exp(-x), d(x*exp(-x), x)], [x, 0, 6], legend: ["f", "f'"])
#% output
#= image("plot.files/plot-9.png")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `list_plot`, `table`, `n_dsolve`
